From 7d4c50d0fd1a8a44a566977850fec4c74c667b8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Crouse <mail@amz-x.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:21:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Remote Desktop page using GNOME Remote Desktop

Lets the computer's screen be shared and optionally controlled over RDP
through gnome-remote-desktop. The page is only shown when
gnome-remote-desktop's settings schema is installed.

Turning it on sets up what the user daemon needs before it serves RDP: a
self-signed TLS certificate (generated with GnuTLS and stored where GNOME
Settings keeps it), credentials in the keyring (the user name and a random
password unless already set), then enables and starts
gnome-remote-desktop.service.

Based on the idea of #60 by DJABhipHop, ported to GTK4 and the current
SettingsPage layout.

Fixes #56

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
